WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.261 --> 00:00:02.400
- Vanilla Bean.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.233
- [Man] This one is Bay.

00:00:03.233 --> 00:00:05.378
- Baby, Nick, they love you.

00:00:05.378 --> 00:00:06.311
- Yeah.

00:00:06.311 --> 00:00:07.657
- Oh.

00:00:07.657 --> 00:00:09.810
(creaking sign)

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.643
(happy pop music)

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:18.063
- I'm so distracted, I can't
look at this little guy.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.060
- Stuff like this, this
is what I set out to do,

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.160
is just play with puppies all the time.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.500
I think the great thing about acting

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.610
is that you step into
somebody else's shoes

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.250
without suffering the consequences.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.630
- I was the kind of person,
who was like, I was a swimmer.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:34.720
I also really loved art

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.710
and I trained classically
as a vocalist for 10 years.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.300
I watched a Gaga concert,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.430
and I started writing music,
and at the end of that year,

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.510
I auditioned for drama
school and I didn't get in,

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.350
so I decided to do a
deployment of music theater

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:50.370
and then from that I figured
I liked the acting thing.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.620
Anyways, so now I'm here.

00:00:52.757 --> 00:00:56.174
(happy electronic music)

00:00:57.025 --> 00:00:58.365
- What's your drag name?

00:00:58.365 --> 00:00:59.381
- Ooh, yeah.
- 'Cause it's hard, man.

00:00:59.381 --> 00:01:00.260
- That's a good one.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.664
I'd get on board with that, drag name.

00:01:02.664 --> 00:01:04.410
What breed of dog are you?

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.290
- I have a--
- That's pretty good.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.390
- Temporary drag name (mumbles) anyway.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:08.340
- What's your temporary drag name?

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.080
- I don't know if I can
swear on BuzzFeed, so.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.517
- Oh.
- No. No.

00:01:11.517 --> 00:01:12.617
- What is your?
- No.

00:01:12.617 --> 00:01:14.587
- What are you doing?
- No? No.

00:01:14.587 --> 00:01:15.910
(contemplative pop music)

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:18.880
- I hope that this movie
furthers the conversation

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.240
of representation and
inclusiveness and tolerance.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.430
See, your story represented on a screen

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:27.910
is a really powerful thing.

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:30.350
- I think representation is crucial.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:34.030
It's so important to see
people who look like you

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:37.340
and act like you and to see
stories that you can relate to,

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:41.700
because it's what makes you
feel not crazy, or not alone.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.770
This is a story that, it's overdue,

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.430
but I hope that it
normalizes those feelings,

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:49.390
'cause I think it's so
underrepresented in the media

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:51.100
and if you don't see those stories,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.280
you don't understand them.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.600
And then it makes it weird
to be that, and I just,

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.500
I think it takes so
much courage to come out

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.704
and hopefully this film can--

00:01:57.704 --> 00:01:58.537
- He's nibbling on my shoe.

00:01:58.537 --> 00:02:00.880
- Be a talking point to ease that, aw.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:01.713
So cute.

00:02:01.713 --> 00:02:03.040
- There's actually a scene in
the movie, if you watch it,

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.240
there's something that
exactly this happens,

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.822
except the dog's maybe not
quite as cute as this one.

00:02:08.822 --> 00:02:10.053
- I love you so much.

00:02:10.053 --> 00:02:13.373
Little Vanilla Bean, this guy
might have to come with me.

00:02:14.664 --> 00:02:18.158
(serene pop music)

00:02:18.158 --> 00:02:20.390
- I feel like now more than ever is a time

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.570
where you find a community,
whether it's online or,

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.970
you can find people
with like-minded views.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:27.290
Don't be afraid to be vulnerable.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:29.210
- I can't give personal
advice, because like,

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:30.550
everyone's story is different,

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.620
and I've never had to
go through coming out,

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.630
or anything like that.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.770
Knowing that you're not
alone and your friends,

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:40.830
if they're real friends, will
accept you and love you and--

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.260
- Oh, wait now, there,
these guys are not friends.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.395
I'm gonna have to separate you two.

00:02:45.395 --> 00:02:47.241
(upbeat guitar solo music)

00:02:47.241 --> 00:02:48.258
(laughter)

00:02:48.258 --> 00:02:49.091
- Sorry.

00:02:49.091 --> 00:02:51.100
I never fit in, like I was an athlete,

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.490
but I was also musical, and
I was also a super nerd,

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.950
but also like, none of
them ever felt right.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.720
You're conflicting ideas of like,

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.232
you're trying so hard
to be authentically you.

00:02:59.232 --> 00:03:00.065
- Yeah.

00:03:00.065 --> 00:03:01.570
- But at the same time,
you're like, who am I?

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:02.940
And trying to figure that out.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.420
What were you like in high school, Nick?

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.410
- I feel like I was kind of a misfit.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.610
I didn't really belong to any one group.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.310
I've never had to do
anything with puppies before.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.659
This is harder than I
thought it was going to be.

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:15.826
(energetic pop music)

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.450
Don't try and fit in as hard.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.650
Don't be afraid to be vulnerable.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:23.280
And trust your instincts
a little bit more.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.450
High school's a time when
you're trying really hard to

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.330
express yourself, but you
don't always have the tools,

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:31.620
emotional tools to do that.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.640
Just pet puppies.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.480
- My advice would be keep
doing what you're doing,

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.015
'cause I feel like I
wouldn't change anything.

00:03:37.015 --> 00:03:40.280
(upbeat rock music)

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.113
I read it, did you read it?

00:03:41.113 --> 00:03:41.946
- Mm-mm.

00:03:41.946 --> 00:03:42.779
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:42.779 --> 00:03:43.612
- I read it, after, I loved it.

00:03:43.612 --> 00:03:44.680
I was such a fangirl of the book.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.970
I reached out to Becky on
Instagram, and just like fanned.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.580
Here, this is your guy.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.330
Adapting a novel for a film is tricky,

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:53.960
'cause there's backstory
you have to include

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.352
in like an hour and a half.

00:03:55.352 --> 00:03:57.562
♪ Baby don't leave me ♪

00:03:57.562 --> 00:03:59.039
(Katherine laughs)

00:03:59.039 --> 00:04:01.380
If you want a little backstory,
the novel's really great.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:02.680
In the book, they go much more

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.030
into Leah and her insecurities,

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:06.300
and I think that's a really large part

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.738
of what's going on with her.

00:04:07.738 --> 00:04:10.210
Not only the whole emotional journey,

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:11.945
but also how she feels about herself.

00:04:11.945 --> 00:04:13.780
- I got to read the book and

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:15.560
it just added a lot of
depth to these characters,

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:17.620
like maybe this is
because of her background.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.150
She used to be a school counselor,

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.810
but she's really good at
making these characters

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:24.970
three-dimensional and
showing their journey.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:26.190
I think we did justice to it.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:29.110
I hope that, if you liked the
book, you'll like the movie.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:30.690
And if you've never read the book,

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.133
I highly recommend checking it out.

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:36.703
(cheerful rock music)

00:04:36.703 --> 00:04:38.290
- We went to Savannah, which was cool,

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.960
except for the Ghost Tour,
I did not enjoy that.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.697
- Oh, yeah, Savannah was
actually the best part of that.

